usage: eval_unet.py [-h] --model MODEL --manifest MANIFEST --report REPORT
                    [--backend {auto,pytorch,onnx,x5}]
                    [--backbone {resnet18,resnet34,resnet50,resnet101,resnet152}]
                    [--limit LIMIT] [--progress-every PROGRESS_EVERY]
                    [--min-miou MIN_MIOU]

Evaluate UNet ResNet checkpoints, ONNX models, or X5 binaries on VOC pairs.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL         .pth, .onnx, or X5 .bin model
  --manifest MANIFEST   image<TAB>mask VOC pair list
  --report REPORT       new JSON report path
  --backend {auto,pytorch,onnx,x5}
                        inference backend; auto selects it from the model
                        suffix
  --backbone {resnet18,resnet34,resnet50,resnet101,resnet152}
                        required for .pth checkpoints and custom-named .bin
                        artifacts
  --limit LIMIT         evaluate only the first N samples
  --progress-every PROGRESS_EVERY
                        print progress every N samples
  --min-miou MIN_MIOU   return 2 below this mIoU
